.TH qgpkg-sign "1" "Sep 2026" "Gentoo Foundation" "qgpkg-sign"
.SH NAME
qgpkg-sign \- sign or re-sign a gpkg binary package (gpkg-sign port)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qgpkg-sign
\fI[opts] <gpkg file>\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fIqgpkg-sign\fR signs a \fBgpkg\fR binary package file, as a C
reimplementation of Portage's \fBgpkg\-sign\fR.
.P
Binary packages will be signed by given GnuPG command. The base
command is defined in the \fIBINPKG_GPG_SIGNING_BASE_COMMAND\fR
variable and will be used for all signing operations;
\fB[PORTAGE_CONFIG]\fR is replaced under different operations.  The
GnuPG key ID used to sign binary packages is set in
\fIBINPKG_GPG_SIGNING_KEY\fR and must exist in
\fIBINPKG_GPG_SIGNING_GPG_HOME\fR. See \fBmake.conf\fR(5).
.P
The \fBPackages\fR index is not updated; run \fBemaint binhost
\-\-fix\fR or \fBqmaint\fR(1) \fIbinhost \-f\fR afterwards.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-k\fR, \fB\-\-keep\-current\-signature\fR
Keep existing signature when updating signature.
.TP
\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-allow\-unsigned\fR
Allow signing from unsigned packages when binpkg-request-signature is enabled.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-skip\-signed\fR
Skip signing if a package is already signed.
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<arg>\fR
Set the ROOT env var.
.TP
\fB\-\-overlay\fR \fI<arg>\fR
Select the given overlay for use, instead of all found (see q -o).
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Report full package versions, emit more elaborate output.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Tighter output; suppress warnings.
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-nocolor\fR
Don't output color.
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR
Force color in output.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print this help and exit.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version and exit.

